<section class="page-head"><span class="eyebrow">Case Studies</span><h1>How I think, shown through work</h1></section>
<section class="cs"><nav class="cs-list" aria-label="Case Studies"><a href="#last-mile" data-id="last-mile">Last mile network</a><a href="#emission" data-id="emission">Emission norms compliant machine</a><a href="#data" data-id="data">Data driven decisions</a><a href="#ai" data-id="ai">AI capability and skills</a></nav><div><article class="cs-panel" id="p-last-mile"><h2>Last mile network</h2><p class="lead">Designed and built from the ground up.</p><h4>Challenge</h4><p>Get products to the final customer reliably, and keep that working as demand grows.</p><h4>What I did</h4><ul><li>Mapped the flow from dispatch to final delivery and found where it broke</li><li>Designed the network structure and the operating routine around it</li><li>Tracked service performance with data so the network could keep improving</li></ul><h4>Why it matters</h4><p>A network that scales means growth does not break delivery.</p></article><article class="cs-panel" id="p-emission"><h2>Emission norms compliant machine</h2><p class="lead">Designed and developed from concept to launch readiness.</p><h4>Challenge</h4><p>Meet emission regulations without losing performance or control of cost.</p><h4>What I did</h4><ul><li>Translated regulatory requirements into design decisions</li><li>Coordinated engineering and suppliers under stage gate timelines</li><li>Kept performance and cost in balance while meeting the norm</li></ul><h4>Why it matters</h4><p>Compliance is a launch gate. Getting it right early saves rework later.</p></article><article class="cs-panel" id="p-data"><h2>Data driven decisions</h2><p class="lead">Metrics and reporting that set the priorities.</p><h4>Challenge</h4><p>Decisions led by opinion give uneven results.</p><h4>What I did</h4><ul><li>Defined the few metrics that matter for each decision</li><li>Built reporting that makes problems visible early</li><li>Turned analysis into clear actions with owners</li></ul><h4>Why it matters</h4><p>When the data sets the priorities, the team knows the next step.</p></article><article class="cs-panel" id="p-ai"><h2>AI capability and skills</h2><p class="lead">I use AI as a working tool, not a buzzword.</p><h4>Challenge</h4><p>Get from messy data to a decision faster, without trusting output blindly.</p><h4>AI capability</h4><ul><li>Analyze and summarize large sets of operational data quickly</li><li>Draft reports, documents and communication</li><li>Automate repeated steps in a workflow</li><li>Build simple AI assistants, like the one on this site</li></ul><h4>AI skills</h4><div class="chipsx"><span>Prompt design</span><span>AI assisted analysis</span><span>Workflow automation</span><span>Reviewing AI output</span><span>Building assistants</span><span>Responsible use</span></div><h4>Why it matters</h4><p>AI proposes, I verify, the data decides.</p></article></div></section>
<footer>Danish Khan · Mannheim, Germany</footer></div>
